A||||3||JohnnyK||Wires... ||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||11-10-2000||02:19 PM||||I have not changed the plug wires of my car yet and have no idea when the last owner did. My problem is hard starting, real rich (almost like not all cylinders are going), etc. I have just finished putting the cradle back in (well, almost) so I'm going to try timing and all that jazz, but would new wires make that much of a difference? Also, does it matter if I get el cheapos? It's only an 85 2.5.. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||11-10-2000||06:01 PM||||Depends how bad the your plug wires are now, of course.  Might want to test them first - visual inspect for cracks, test resistance with an ohmmeter while you flex them.  Run car with hood open in the dark and watch for sparks.   <P>On the other hand, if they're pretty old, and you want to replace them, go ahead and do it.  They don't have to be expensive to be good - but I'd go with a brand you've heard of.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-10-2000||06:15 PM||||If it's been more than a year or 3 just replace them and be done with it. The cap and rotor as well if you don't know how old these parts are they are likely too old.<P>The Borg Warner wires carried by Pep Boys and others work well on the 4. They aren't very expesncive for helical core wires. (They run beautifully on my DIS motor wich puts out way more energy then HEI.)||||reg||1
Z||000003||strdream||11-10-2000||07:49 PM||||Make sure that your foot is compleatly Off the gas peddle. Even a little too much TPS (Throtle Position Sensor) voltage will flood it. You can check your TPS voltage. There are three wires, one is ground one is 5 volt referance (key on only) and one is signal. at an idle your signal voltage should be less than one volt. If you have adjusted your idle speed by adjusting the set screw, you may have messed up the idle voltage. Re-adjust TPS.  Next go to the Engine Coolant Temp sensor (ECT) if it is disconnected or "open" the ECM thinks that it is -44 degrees and it will give it lots of fuel. I would check that first actualy.<P>Ross   ||||reg||1
